# Pingdom Website Speed Test — SELPIC homepage learning

Fixture: Pingdom Tools on **`http://www.selpic.com.au/`** (report pasted 2026-09-17).

## Snapshot (as reported)

| Metric | Value |
|--------|------:|
| Performance grade | **C 73** |
| Page size | **489.7 KB** |
| Load time | **187 ms** |
| Requests | **31** |
| 200 OK | 30 |
| 308 redirect | 1 |
| “Error” type | **5** (~60.9 KB) |

Top Pingdom suggestions: **F0 gzip**, **F0 Expires**, **F32 fewer HTTP requests**. A100 on empty src, JS at bottom, DOM, favicon.

## How to read this tool (vs PSI)

| Pingdom | Reality for SELPIC |
|---------|-------------------|
| ~490 KB / 187 ms | **Synthetic / shallow** — often misses heavy hero MP4, CMS images, post-load catalog. Not comparable to PSI mobile ~**3.2 MiB** / LCP ~4s. |
| Grade C73 | YSlow-era rules, not Core Web Vitals. |
| Tested **`http://`** | Forces **308 → https** (seen in report). Prefer **`https://www.selpic.com.au/`** for retests. |

**Do not** chase Pingdom C→A as the storefront KPI. Keep **PageSpeed Insights mobile** as the primary lab score (see `storefront-mobile-performance.mdc`).

## F0 “Compress with gzip” — usually false positive

Live HTML responds with **`Content-Encoding: br`** (Brotli) on Vercel when `Accept-Encoding` allows it.

Pingdom historically grades only **gzip** and under-credits Brotli → **F0** even when compression is on and better than gzip.

**Do not** force `Content-Encoding: gzip` in `vercel.json` / Next headers (double-compress risk).

## F0 “Add Expires headers” — outdated rule + our Expires: 0

Modern caching uses **`Cache-Control`**, not `Expires`.

Verified:

- `/_next/static/…` → `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` (**correct**)
- `/images/…` → `max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=…` (**correct**)
- Catch-all in `next.config.js` also sets **`Expires: 0`** (and HTML `no-store` by design for CMS-driven home)

Pingdom still wants far-future **Expires** on static files. Optional later: stop emitting `Expires: 0` on `/_next/static` / `/images` only (leave HTML no-store). **Not required** for browsers that honor Cache-Control.

## Error bucket (5 × ~404 HTML ≈ 60.9 KB)

Each Next 404 page is ~**15–16 KB** (br). Five of them ≈ Pingdom’s **Error 60.9 KB**.

Likely leftover probes (code paths mostly cleaned 2026-09-16; verify HAR for exact URLs):

- `/logo.svg`, `/images/logo.svg` (old fallbacks)
- `/manifest.json`, `/site.webmanifest` (not shipped)
- possibly one more stale chunk / icon

**Action when owner asks:** download Pingdom HAR → list the five Error URLs → remove references or add assets. Do not invent a PWA manifest only to silence Pingdom.

## F32 “Fewer HTTP requests”

~**20 script** chunks is normal for Next App Router code-split. Further merging can hurt caching. Prefer existing `dynamic()` / no new whole-route client weight on `/`.

## Redirect

`http://` → `https://` **308** is correct (HSTS / Vercel). Always share **https** URLs in marketing and speed tests.

## Favicon / logo in this run

Report shows **`/images/logo.webp` ~12.5 KB** and Inter woff2 ~49.5 KB — aligns with current icon/font setup. Fine.

